<title>UK: U.S. biggest air cargo country market for Manchester.</title>
<headline>U.S. biggest air cargo country market for Manchester.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. was the largest overall country market in terms of combined imports and exports handled at Manchester airport last year, statistics issued by the airport show.</p>
<p>Traffic to and from the U.S. totalled 27,266 tonnes and this was followed by Hong Kong with 20,334 tonnes.</p>
<p>Total cargo handled at Manchester last year at 83,791 tonnes was 1.5 percent down on 1995.</p>
<p>Imports into Manchester were 0.2 percent higher at 41,788 tonnes but this was outweighed by a dip of 3.2 percent in exports to 42,003 tonnes in 1996.</p>
<p>The main country markets (imports and exports combined) in tonnes are:</p>
<p> COUNTRY		1996		 1995</p>
<p> U.S.		  27,266	     23,896</p>
<p> HONG HONG	   20,334	     20,359</p>
<p> NETHERLANDS	  5,544	     10,673</p>
<p> IRELAND		4,446		3,880</p>
<p> GERMANY		3,464		4,128</p>
<p> UAE		    3,157		5,258</p>
<p> SINGAPORE	    3,156		2,604</p>
<p> SWITZERLAND	  2,938		1,723</p>
<p> UK		     2,653		2,516</p>
<p> CANADA		 2,188		1,676</p>
<p> FRANCE		 1,668		1,763</p>
<p> PAKISTAN	     1,319		1,707</p>
<p> SPAIN		  1,035		  763</p>
<p>(inc Canary Islands)</p>
